Fillets: a ball turning about the end of the edge it rolls on is released
where a step lands on the point of its tangency with the edge (mitcad#343).

The case: 0905's notch wall, on a body a few micrometres off the one
there. The ball turns about the vertex between the wall's far edges
(0170's pivot) until it is tangent to the next edge, where the blend ends
and the next one, rolling on that edge, starts. The walk's step landed on
that point: the ball's side of the edge there came out -5e-14, so the
release (side > 0) was not taken; at the next step, past the point, the
release was solved back at the point before, whose parameter equals the
last point's but for rounding, and the exact comparison took it for a
point behind the walk. The steps shrank to nothing, the piece ended with
its contact on no edge, the next piece did not roll on the next edge, and
the stripe failed.

- BRepBlend_SurfRstLineBuilder::InternalPerform: the release is looked for
  where the side is within Precision::Confusion() of the release, and the
  release point is taken within Precision::PConfusion() of the walk's last
  point and of the step.

Upstream: new.

